		(uuid "e73b0bde-80ec-4417-b60a-87a44b598499")
	)
	(text "COMPUTE (STAMP-P4)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 186.69 245.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "eca9c67d-bd61-42a7-a478-edbc1f4f0f64")
	)
	(text "MOTOR SWITCH (record section 4). TPS48111 datasheet Figure 9-14 topology:\n  back-to-back N-FETs, common source, pre-charge through Q403 and Q402's body\n  diode.\nOpen = open both ways: back-drive never reaches the board, so the regen shunt\n  sizes for the powered 6.8 W case.  FETs Q401/Q402: 100 V (58.6 V back-EMF),\n  D2PAK class; TODO pick part.\nR401 2 mOhm: 30 mV at 15 A. OC R404 39.2k = 15.2 A for 10 ms (C402 680n, R405\n  100k = LATCH-OFF; firmware re-arms by toggling MOTOR_EN). SC R403 3.4k = 30\n  A in 1.2 us.\nIMON R406 8.25k: 3.0 V at 20 A into an ADC1 pin.  CBST C401 470n.  UVLO\n  R407/R408 470k/24.9k: on above ~23 V.  Q404 sits beside Q401/Q402 in layout:\n  150 C cutoff.\nMOTOR_EN floats during P4 boot: R409 pulldown + internal pulldown = off.\n  INA_ALERT_N (open drain) pulls EN low: INA228 limits cut the motor with no\n  MCU.\nPRE-CHARGE: drive input measured 150 uF (hw-x65). PRECHARGE_EN high ~75 ms\n  (R412 100R, 0.36 A peak, ~0.1 J), then MOTOR_EN high, then PRECHARGE_EN low.\nD401 SMBJ48CA: stands off above the 45 V clamp, clamps under the 100 V FETs;\n  catches the hot-plug ring of the drive's ceramic input."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 718.82 391.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f2366600-62d6-40c0-becc-a0eab5331d07")
	)
	(text "COMPUTE (record section 8; SPEC: no RP2350, the P4 LP core emits quadrature).\n  Stamp-P4 + Stamp-AddOn C6 stacked on\n  top (SDIO G42-G48, not castellated).\nFixed pins only: VIN (14) from +5V, the stamp ORs it with its own USB-C 5V and makes\n  SOC_3.3V itself; all GND pads.\n  No reset button: CHIP_EN and G35 go to tweezer pads TP901 / TP903 beside GND pad\n    TP902 (stamp has 10k pull-ups).\nG35 appears on pads 36 AND 48 in M5's own symbol and schematic: both wired to\n  P4_BOOT.\nPIN ASSIGNMENT FOLLOWS LAYOUT (operator ruling): each function net below gets the\n  stamp pad nearest its circuit\n  once parts are placed.\n  QUAD_A, QUAD_B          LP GPIO (LPG0-15) for the LP-core emitter; avoid LPG14/15\n    (LP UART console)\n  I2C_SDA, I2C_SCL        LPG11 / LPG9 are the module I2C (shared with the add-on\n    connector; SPEC open item)\n  RS485_TX, RS485_RX, RS485_DE   any HP GPIO via the matrix (UART RS485 half-duplex\n    mode)\n  MOTOR_EN, PRECHARGE_EN, MSW_FLT_N, INA_ALERT_N, CLAMP_MON, DRV_ALM, DRV_RDY,\n    FAN_PWM, FAN_TACH, LED_DATA,\n    BTN_HOME, BTN_PAIR\n  MSW_IMON, THERM, SHUNT_TEMP   ADC1 (G16-G23)\n  Avoid straps: G34 (JTAG enable), G35 (boot), G36, G37/G38 (UART0 console). Buttons\n    NEVER on a strap: a button\n    held at power-on must reach firmware, not the ROM.\nD5 status pixel: LED_DATA -> AHCT125 gate 3 (Drive IO) -> LED_DIN at 5 V (WS2812B\n  VIH = 0.7 VDD).\nSW1 HOME: press = home, hold = reset (firmware, on release). SW2 PAIR: hold = pair,\n  held at power-on = AP config\n  mode, press TBD. Both use the P4's internal pull-ups.\nRescue: short TP901 (EN) to TP902 = reset; hold TP903 (BOOT) to TP902 while\n  resetting = ROM download mode (USB\n  flashing enters it on its own)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 718.82 302.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f575d6f4-6928-4f82-954f-8eed46ac9732")
	)
